-- READY scaffold only: this non-runnable reservation contains no executable
-- Client archive assertion and is excluded by root run-all *.sql discovery.
--
-- Implementation must retain this `.ready` marker byte-for-byte while adding a
-- separately registered runnable `.sql` test leaf. It must prove account-bound
-- OperationID validation; exact/changed/lost-response replay; cross-command reuse
-- refusal; active exact-revision apply; already-archived and stale/future/out-of-
-- signed-range conflict; signed-bigint exhaustion; true same-revision one-apply/
-- one-conflict concurrency; and archive/create-Project serialization on the same
-- Client lock with both orderings, durable project_setup_client_not_selectable,
-- no post-archive Project success and no deadlock.
-- The shared result table must reserve `client-archive-`: non-archive commands
-- cannot squat the prefix, and cross-Account/cross-command results neither
-- disclose nor rebind Client archive identity.
-- It must prove monotonic revision/time, exact mutation columns, byte-identical
-- Client identity/name/creation audit and every currently represented Project/
-- related/history row, plus a no-cascade/no-related-write SQL boundary. Every
-- later related table must add the same preservation regression.
-- Owner success, restricted/revoked/anonymous/actor-mismatch/cross-Account denial,
-- auth-first non-enumeration, direct-write denial, immutable result scope and no
-- restore/delete/rename/merge/reassignment/cascade behavior are mandatory.
